NAME
       mandb - rebuild the index used by man -k and whatis

SYNOPSIS
       mandb

DESCRIPTION
       mandb reads the manual pages under /usr/share/man and rebuilds the
       index that man -k, apropos and whatis search. A daily job does this
       automatically; run it by hand (as root) right after installing
       software when man -k does not find the new pages yet.

EXAMPLES
           mandb
           man -k vsftpd

SEE ALSO
       man(1), apropos(1), whatis(1)
